# LF everywhere: the index and every checkout.
#
# A Windows CI runner checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default, which turned
# every text file into CRLF there and broke byte-level comparisons on the runner
# while passing locally: generated docs, the pinned film-doc SHA-256, template page
# HTML, and the AcpClient shell-quoting test all failed for that one reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binaries: never normalize, never try to diff text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
